            <ArticleTitle>Scintigraphic diagnosis of right ventricular ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>407-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a patient with exercise induced right ventricular ischemia demonstrated on stress TI-201 myocardial scintiscan. The patient underwent cardiac catheterization, and subtotal occlusion was found at the proximal right coronary artery. Repeat stress TI-201 scan became normal following the successful percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
